//! fail
//! flags: --ownership-check
//! error-any: ownership proof is incomplete
// D17.19: a call of extern exit is the final normal-exit boundary, and each owning global must
// be empty there. `cache` holds the allocation of this body on each path to the call, so the
// exit loses it. No fort call stands on the path, so a witness path validates the loss. No call
// of std.rt.shutdown empties args_store first, so that owner stays unproved.
import std.libc;

u8 mut@ own mut cache = {};

fn main() i32 {
    del(cache);
    cache = new(u8, 8);
    libc.exit(0); //! error: lost ownership of 'cache'
}
